<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Béla I of Hungary</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1016–<a href="/years/1063">1063</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Béla I was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> from 1060 to 1063. The younger brother of Andrew I, he returned from exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> and in 1048 received a third of the kingdom as a duchy, the tercia pars regni. When Andrew named his infant son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/solomon">Solomon</a> as heir, Béla rebelled with Polish help, defeated him and took the crown, but died in 1063 after the collapse of his throne canopy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bela-i-of-hungary.jpg" alt="Béla I of Hungary" width="320" height="373" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Johannes de Thurocz · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Thur%C3%B3czy_kr%C3%B3nika_-_I._B%C3%A9la_kir%C3%A1ly.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
